    <string name="guide_heading">Capture. Count. Prepare.</string>
    <string name="guide_intro">Frames, markers and calculations update together.</string>
    <string name="guide_acquire_title">Capture a clear grid</string>
    <string name="guide_acquire">Align the camera with the microscope eyepiece. Adjust focus and illumination to show the cells and grid rulings. Images can also be imported from the photo library.</string>
    <string name="guide_frame_title">Align and count</string>
    <string name="guide_frame">Grid boundaries are located automatically. Drag the eight handles or the whole frame, and use 1/5 px controls for fine adjustments. Pinch to zoom. Central-grid recognition offers an RBC shortcut while keeping all counting modes available.</string>
    <string name="guide_modes_title">Improved Neubauer modes</string>
    <string name="guide_modes">4×: full 3×3 mm grid, with all nine squares or a selection. 10×: separate images of A1, A3, C1 and C3; concentration uses the mean of the counted corners. RBC: central 1 mm² grid with 5×5 groups; the four corners and center cover 0.2 mm². Custom mode uses the entered physical area.</string>
    <string name="guide_rules_title">Boundary and cluster rules</string>
    <string name="guide_rules">Include objects touching top/left boundaries and exclude those touching bottom/right boundaries. Triple-line bundles use their middle ruling. Each connected cluster counts as one object.</string>
    <string name="guide_parameters_title">Tune with live results</string>
    <string name="guide_parameters">Sensitivity adapts to local noise. Auto appearance combines bright and dark support; Dark and Bright select one polarity. Change automatic/manual size settings while viewing markers, counts and calculations. Use Add, Delete and Undo for marker edits.</string>
    <string name="guide_formula_title">Concentration and volume</string>
    <string name="guide_formula">Sampled volume = area × depth / 1000 mL\nConcentration = count × dilution / sampled volume\nTotal cells = concentration × stock volume\nRequired volume = target / concentration × 1000 µL\n\nAt 0.1 mm depth, corner-square concentration is the mean count × dilution × 10⁴ cells/mL. A 1:1 stock/stain mixture has dilution factor 2.</string>
    <string name="guide_records_title">Save, export and reset</string>
    <string name="guide_records">Samples retain PNG images, markers, selected squares and parameters. Export creates a CSV report and annotated PNG images. Chamber reset restores area, depth 0.1 mm, dilution 2 and stock volume 1 mL. Detection settings have their own Reset control.</string>
